[- Concept: CXPath. -]
[page id='cxpath'
  [meta
    title='CXPath'
    layout='concept'
    nav-order='230'
    audience='learner'
    summary='The query language inside CXL directives — XPath-shaped, CX-native.'
  ]

  [section id='what' title='What CXPath Is'
    [prose CXPath is the query language CXL uses inside directives. Where XPath queries an XML tree, CXPath queries a CXDM tree. The surface is familiar to anyone who has written XPath — paths, predicates, axes, and a substantial XPath 3.1 and 4.0 function library all available.]
  ]

  [section id='paths' title='Paths'
    [prose Paths look like Unix paths but walk the document tree. Double-slash matches any depth; single slash walks a direct step; the at-sigil prefixes an attribute lookup.]
    [code lang='cx' src='''//pizza                  # all pizza elements at any depth
//menu/pizza             # pizza elements that are direct children of menu
//pizza/@name            # attribute name of every pizza
//pizza/topping/@name    # walk down two steps, then read an attribute''']
  ]

  [section id='predicates' title='Predicates'
    [prose Square brackets after a step filter the matched set. Predicates can compare values, test attribute existence, call functions, use position, or compose with boolean operators.]
    [code lang='cx' src="//pizza[@price > 10]
//item[count(line) > 3]
//user[starts-with(@id, 'admin-')]
//*[local-name() = 'pizza']
//product[@stock > 0 and @price < 20]"]
  ]

  [section id='axes' title='Axes'
    [prose An axis selects nodes by relationship to the context. CX supports the standard XPath axes; the most commonly used are highlighted below.]
    [code lang='cx' src='''child::pizza
descendant::topping
ancestor::menu
parent::*
self::*
following-sibling::*
preceding-sibling::*
attribute::*''']
  ]

  [section id='functions' title='Function Library'
    [prose The XPath function library is substantial. CXPath ships the working subset of XPath 3.1 and 4.0; common members: count, sum, max, min, position, last, string-length, substring, contains, starts-with, ends-with, lower-case, upper-case, normalize-space, local-name, name, namespace-uri.]
    [code lang='cx' src='''//item[@count = max(//item/@count)]
[?= string-length(//page/@title)]
//user[contains(@email, '@example.com')]''']
  ]

  [section id='operators' title='Operators'
    [prose CXPath includes operators beyond comparison: arithmetic (plus, minus, times, divide, mod), boolean (and, or, not), set (union, intersect, except), and the range operator (to).]
    [code lang='cx' src='''[?for n :in 1 to 10 :return [slot id=[?= n]]]
//pizza | //side                # union: pizzas and sides
//item[@price * 1.08 > 20]      # price plus tax > 20''']
  ]

  [section id='variables' title='Variables'
    [prose Variables introduced by ?for or ?let are referenced with the dollar-sign sigil. Most expressions allow the bare variable name; the dollar-sign form is required when the context is ambiguous (collection-slot text, predicate RHS).]
    [code lang='cx' src='''[?for it :in //item :return
  [?for ex :in //example :where ex/@id = it/@id :return
    [match item-id=[?= it/@id]]]]''']
  ]

  [section id='related' title='Related'
    [list
      [item path='reference/cxl'         label='CXL — directives that embed CXPath']
      [item path='reference/cxpath'      label='CXPath function reference']
      [item path='tour/programs'         label='50 Ways to Love Your CXL Code — CXPath in context']
    ]
  ]

  [preserve id='author-notes'
    [- Empty by default. -]
  ]
]
